WEBVTT

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.366
Last time,
on Star Trek: Voyager...

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.135
Looks like
this entire part of space

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.147
has changed somehow.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.342
We should dismantle this weapon

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.976
and rejoin our people.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:21.385
No, not until every colony...

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.479
every individual...

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.250
every blade of grass
is restored.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.656
It appears that someone...

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:29.662
or something
has altered history.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.830
Captain, that energy beam...

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.739
it's pushing Voyager
out of the space-time continuum.

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:45.677
He's trying to erase us
from history.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.740
I promised myself that I
would never give this order,

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:54.219
that I would never break up
this family,

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.051
but asking you to stay...

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.621
would be asking you to die.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.561
And now, the conclusion.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:13.099
Captain's Log, Stardate 51425.4.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.472
Our condition has left us
vulnerable to spatial anomalies

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:20.343
and to any alien species
eager for a piece of hardware.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.315
We've taken refuge
in a class-9 nebula.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.390
Oh, come on!

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:36.725
Don't do this to me now.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.492
Emergency force fields
are holding.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.658
How the hell did all this gas
get inside?

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.032
Looks like a malfunction
in the ventilation system.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.144
Okay, I'm going to try

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:58.116
reversing the osmotic pressure
on this deck.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.846
- Oh!
- Whoa!

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.581
The gas corroded
the circuit relays.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.250
Let's bypass.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:10.653
We've got three minutes
of air left.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.494
How long can you
hold your breath?

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.295
Ensign Kim found time
to be treated, so can you.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.398
How is Harry?

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.466
He'll be fine, but I'm surprised
he didn't asphyxiate.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.339
I told you eight minutes
on that deck,

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.972
not eight and a half,
not nine, and certainly not 12.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.948
Would you rather have
an indoor nebula?

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.314
If we didn't stop it
then and there,

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.943
it would have flooded
another two decks.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.078
B'Elanna, engines?

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.087
Not yet, Captain.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.713
One of the warp nacelles
is still off-line.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:37.814
The other one's a lost cause.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.882
Route all available power
to the good one.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.153
The alveoli in your lungs
have been chemically burned.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:45.323
I want you off your feet
for the next 48 hours.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.026
Impossible. I've got
too much work to do.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.761
There are seven
other crew members on board.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.701
You're the Captain.
Delegate.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:51.931
Inject me with trioxin.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.495
That should help me
breathe a little easier.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.370
B'Elanna, stand by
for the transfer.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.432
Right.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.376
Trioxin is used
in emergency situations

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.935
as a stopgap measure.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.776
Your lungs have suffered
serious damage.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.145
They need to be treated
properly.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.150
Doctor's orders.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.880
Captain's orders...
trioxin, now.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.444
Aye, aye.

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:09.783
It's your body.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.346
Who am I to judge?

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:12.983
I'm only the Chief
Medical Officer.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.152
What do I know?

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.320
Thank you.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.566
Now, where were we?

00:05:33.998 --> 00:05:35.966
Well...

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.558
you look rested.

00:05:38.769 --> 00:05:40.066
Where's my crewmate?

00:05:40.104 --> 00:05:42.664
He should have been here by now.

00:05:42.706 --> 00:05:44.936
No doubt
he's making himself difficult.

00:05:44.975 --> 00:05:49.469
I've never seen such
an intransigent young man.

00:05:49.513 --> 00:05:51.606
You've had us in isolation
for two months.

00:05:51.649 --> 00:05:53.708
We've been scanned,
poked and prodded.

00:05:53.751 --> 00:05:55.810
How do you expect us to act?

00:05:55.853 --> 00:05:58.720
With some degree
of dignity and restraint.

00:05:58.756 --> 00:06:00.917
Your crewmate has none.

00:06:00.958 --> 00:06:02.550
What do you want from us?

00:06:04.528 --> 00:06:05.654
At the moment...

00:06:05.696 --> 00:06:07.425
information.

00:06:07.531 --> 00:06:09.658
Anything
for such a charming host.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.758
Are you all right?

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:11.825
The galley has prepared

00:06:11.869 --> 00:06:14.337
a selection
of unique delicacies.

00:06:14.371 --> 00:06:16.805
You won't find them
anywhere else in the galaxy.

00:06:16.841 --> 00:06:18.103
Please, join me.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.243
Malkothian spirits...

00:06:28.285 --> 00:06:29.843
an extremely rare vintage.

00:06:29.887 --> 00:06:32.447
The only bottle known to exist.

00:06:32.556 --> 00:06:34.615
Your Captain said that...

00:06:34.658 --> 00:06:36.751
your vessel is trying
to reach home.

00:06:36.794 --> 00:06:39.786
I hadn't realized
how far your home was.

00:06:41.665 --> 00:06:43.690
You're an anomalous component...

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:47.636
alone, disconnected,
impossible to predict.

00:06:49.473 --> 00:06:53.341
You have no idea how you've
complicated my mission.

00:06:53.377 --> 00:06:55.675
Glad to hear it.

00:06:55.713 --> 00:06:58.477
When I first encountered
your vessel,

00:06:58.582 --> 00:07:00.914
it was badly damaged,
barely functioning.

00:07:00.951 --> 00:07:04.250
What if I told you
that, in the blink of an eye,

00:07:04.288 --> 00:07:08.054
I could restore Voyager
to its former condition?

00:07:08.092 --> 00:07:10.720
That you and I
would never have met?

00:07:10.761 --> 00:07:12.126
That you might
even find yourself

00:07:12.162 --> 00:07:14.426
closer to the Alpha Quadrant?

00:07:14.498 --> 00:07:17.433
By using the weapon on this ship
to alter history.

00:07:17.535 --> 00:07:19.093
Yes.

00:07:19.136 --> 00:07:22.071
I can control the destiny
of a...

00:07:22.106 --> 00:07:25.439
single molecule
or an entire civilization.

00:07:25.476 --> 00:07:26.534
How's the wine?

00:07:27.578 --> 00:07:28.545
Excellent.

00:07:28.579 --> 00:07:31.207
This bottle is
the only component left

00:07:31.248 --> 00:07:33.614
of the once powerful
Malkoth race.

00:07:33.651 --> 00:07:35.448
Everything else about them...

00:07:35.486 --> 00:07:37.681
cities, culture,
the very species itself...

00:07:37.721 --> 00:07:39.313
never existed...

00:07:39.356 --> 00:07:40.721
because of me.

00:07:42.126 --> 00:07:46.392
Every dish you see here comes
from a civilization that...

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:48.261
has been erased from time.

00:07:48.299 --> 00:07:51.700
Mr. Paris, you're devouring
the last remnants

00:07:51.735 --> 00:07:54.067
of the Alsuran Empire.

00:07:54.104 --> 00:07:55.969
I have collected artifacts
from...

00:07:57.808 --> 00:08:00.572
hundreds of worlds.

00:08:00.611 --> 00:08:02.738
This vessel is
more than a weapon.

00:08:04.348 --> 00:08:06.748
It's a museum of lost histories.

00:08:09.753 --> 00:08:13.780
You two gentlemen almost became
artifacts yourselves.

00:08:15.326 --> 00:08:17.658
But I've decided to...

00:08:17.695 --> 00:08:19.390
spare your vessel.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.658
Why?

00:08:20.698 --> 00:08:22.598
Call it an act of compassion.

00:08:22.633 --> 00:08:24.225
You're trying to reach home.

00:08:24.268 --> 00:08:25.895
In a way, so am I.

00:08:27.905 --> 00:08:30.703
We can work together
to achieve both our goals.

00:08:30.741 --> 00:08:33.039
What do you propose?

00:08:33.077 --> 00:08:35.671
In order to make
the calculations required

00:08:35.713 --> 00:08:36.907
to restore Voyager,

00:08:36.947 --> 00:08:39.711
I need to know
about some of your experiences

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.047
in this Quadrant...

00:08:41.085 --> 00:08:42.450
what species
you interacted with,

00:08:42.486 --> 00:08:45.080
how other components were
affected by your presence...

00:08:45.122 --> 00:08:47.352
You can't find her, can you?

00:08:47.391 --> 00:08:49.825
I think Captain Janeway
has been eluding you

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:51.054
for the past two months.

00:08:51.095 --> 00:08:53.996
Otherwise, you would've
destroyed Voyager by now.

00:08:55.032 --> 00:08:57.466
I'm offering you
a way out of this situation.

00:08:57.534 --> 00:09:00.059
You accept my offer...

00:09:01.405 --> 00:09:03.999
or when I do find Voyager,
I will destroy it.

00:09:04.041 --> 00:09:07.033
And how many civilizations
will you have to erase

00:09:07.077 --> 00:09:08.908
to send us merrily on our way?

00:09:08.946 --> 00:09:10.106
No, thanks.

00:09:10.147 --> 00:09:11.910
We don't want that kind
of blood on our hands.

00:09:11.949 --> 00:09:13.974
Tom, hold on.

00:09:15.953 --> 00:09:17.386
You said you could control

00:09:17.421 --> 00:09:19.286
the destiny
of a single molecule.

00:09:19.323 --> 00:09:22.087
If you made
a precise enough calculation,

00:09:22.126 --> 00:09:25.425
could you restore Voyager
without harming anyone?

00:09:25.529 --> 00:09:27.394
It is possible...

00:09:27.431 --> 00:09:29.160
but it's extremely difficult.

00:09:29.199 --> 00:09:31.292
That's why I need
your cooperation.

00:09:32.569 --> 00:09:34.628
I'd rather spend a year
in solitary confinement

00:09:34.672 --> 00:09:35.832
than listen to any of this.

00:09:35.873 --> 00:09:36.840
Tom, have a seat.

00:09:36.874 --> 00:09:38.967
Chakotay, we can't trust him.

00:09:39.009 --> 00:09:40.909
You're correct.

00:09:40.944 --> 00:09:44.141
Given the circumstances,
there is no reason to trust me,

00:09:44.181 --> 00:09:46.012
but trust isn't necessary.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:47.608
We need each other.

00:09:50.788 --> 00:09:53.154
Obrist...

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.353
show our guest
to his new quarters.

00:09:56.393 --> 00:09:57.690
I'll do everything in my power

00:09:57.728 --> 00:09:59.696
to make you comfortable here,
Mr. Paris.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.062
All I ask in return...

00:10:02.099 --> 00:10:04.499
is that you keep an open mind.

00:10:15.913 --> 00:10:18.040
I was very impressed
with your question.

00:10:18.082 --> 00:10:21.017
You seem to understand
the subtleties of time.

00:10:22.486 --> 00:10:25.922
Professor Vassbinder
might've disagreed with you.

00:10:25.956 --> 00:10:27.981
I failed his course
in temporal mechanics.

00:10:29.226 --> 00:10:32.457
Beyond study
and instrumentation,

00:10:32.496 --> 00:10:33.929
there is instinct.

00:10:35.466 --> 00:10:40.233
Not everyone has the ability
to truly perceive time...

00:10:41.371 --> 00:10:44.272
its colors, its moods.

00:10:47.177 --> 00:10:48.872
Perhaps you do.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.407
I'm certainly willing
to give it a try.

00:10:55.119 --> 00:10:56.245
To distant friends.

00:10:56.286 --> 00:10:57.310
To friends.

00:10:57.354 --> 00:10:58.321
Hear, hear.

00:10:58.355 --> 00:10:59.344
Cheers.

00:11:09.566 --> 00:11:11.124
Well?

00:11:14.538 --> 00:11:16.199
Interesting.

00:11:17.508 --> 00:11:18.805
Not bad.

00:11:18.842 --> 00:11:20.139
Not bad at all.

00:11:20.177 --> 00:11:22.771
What... is it exactly?

00:11:22.813 --> 00:11:25.782
I call it "the elixir
of endurance."

00:11:25.816 --> 00:11:27.807
It's loaded with amino acids,
carbohydrates...

00:11:27.851 --> 00:11:29.751
all the nutrients
necessary for the crew

00:11:29.787 --> 00:11:31.755
to withstand these
stressful conditions.

00:11:31.789 --> 00:11:33.086
Ration cubes.

00:11:33.123 --> 00:11:37.059
Well, yes, yes,
but this time, pureed

00:11:37.094 --> 00:11:38.083
and mixed with water

00:11:38.128 --> 00:11:39.925
and enhanced
with Talaxian spices.

00:11:39.963 --> 00:11:41.260
It is offensive.

00:11:42.666 --> 00:11:44.429
Fortunately,
taste is irrelevant.

00:11:44.468 --> 00:11:46.493
Well, it's been a few days

00:11:46.603 --> 00:11:48.503
since we've gathered
in one place.

00:11:48.572 --> 00:11:50.403
Now's a good time to catch up.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:51.930
How are the repairs proceeding?

00:11:51.975 --> 00:11:53.203
I'm happy to report

00:11:53.243 --> 00:11:56.178
that I've repaired the optronic
error in my program.

00:11:56.213 --> 00:11:58.681
And the power grid.

00:11:58.715 --> 00:12:00.945
We're operating
at 32 percent efficiency.

00:12:00.984 --> 00:12:04.078
I think I can bring it up to 50,
but I'll need a few more days.

00:12:04.121 --> 00:12:05.179
Warp drive.

00:12:05.222 --> 00:12:08.191
I'm still having trouble
with the starboard nacelle.

00:12:08.225 --> 00:12:09.192
How long?

00:12:09.226 --> 00:12:11.751
Three weeks, minimum.

00:12:15.732 --> 00:12:17.723
I thought this nebula
would be a safe haven

00:12:17.768 --> 00:12:18.996
until we finished repairs,

00:12:19.036 --> 00:12:21.129
but it's turning
into a permanent residence.

00:12:21.171 --> 00:12:23.969
We've got to get back
into open space,

00:12:24.007 --> 00:12:25.372
find allies,

00:12:25.409 --> 00:12:28.845
put together a fighting force
to take on Annorax.

00:12:31.215 --> 00:12:34.207
We're leaving this damn cloud
first thing tomorrow morning.

00:12:34.251 --> 00:12:37.015
Captain, you are in error.

00:12:38.088 --> 00:12:39.350
Really?

00:12:39.389 --> 00:12:41.880
At the moment,
this vessel is defenseless.

00:12:41.925 --> 00:12:42.914
We should remain here

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.860
until we are functioning
at our peak efficiency.

00:12:44.895 --> 00:12:48.490
I appreciate your opinion,
Seven, but I disagree.

00:12:48.532 --> 00:12:52.127
We leave tomorrow, 0800 hours.

00:12:54.703 --> 00:12:56.967
It is inappropriate
to contradict the Captain

00:12:57.005 --> 00:12:58.199
in front of the crew.

00:12:58.240 --> 00:12:59.502
That was not my intention.

00:12:59.541 --> 00:13:02.066
I simply pointed out
that her decision was wrong.

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:03.372
In your view.

00:13:03.412 --> 00:13:04.709
And yours.

00:13:04.746 --> 00:13:06.407
I know you well enough
to say that.

00:13:06.448 --> 00:13:07.574
Then you should also know

00:13:07.616 --> 00:13:10.084
that my trust
in Captain Janeway is absolute.

00:13:10.118 --> 00:13:13.315
The decision you or I
might have made is irrelevant.

00:13:13.355 --> 00:13:16.051
As a Borg, I submitted
to a single authority...

00:13:16.091 --> 00:13:17.285
the collective.

00:13:17.326 --> 00:13:19.817
Over the past several months,
I've been encouraged

00:13:19.861 --> 00:13:21.453
to think and act
as an individual.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:25.330
It is difficult to know
when to restrain myself.

00:13:25.367 --> 00:13:26.959
Remember this guideline:

00:13:27.002 --> 00:13:29.061
The Captain is always right.

00:13:29.104 --> 00:13:32.073
Even when you know
her logic is flawed?

00:13:33.775 --> 00:13:35.140
Perhaps.

00:13:44.486 --> 00:13:48.855
Component 37329... a rogue comet.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.482
About eight months ago,

00:13:50.559 --> 00:13:51.992
Voyager made
a course correction

00:13:52.027 --> 00:13:53.016
to avoid the comet.

00:13:53.061 --> 00:13:55.461
According to my calculations,

00:13:55.497 --> 00:13:57.965
it led to our entering
Krenim space.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.797
Your solution, then, would be

00:13:59.835 --> 00:14:01.826
to erase that comet
from history.

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:03.167
Exactly.

00:14:03.205 --> 00:14:05.173
Voyager would have
stayed on its course

00:14:05.207 --> 00:14:07.402
and bypassed Krenim
space altogether.

00:14:07.442 --> 00:14:09.842
Sounds simple enough.

00:14:09.878 --> 00:14:11.436
Conduct a simulation.

00:14:12.514 --> 00:14:14.141
Temporal incursion in progress.

00:14:24.192 --> 00:14:25.921
What happened?

00:14:25.961 --> 00:14:27.986
Had you actually
eradicated that comet,

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:31.989
all life within 50 light-years
would never have existed.

00:14:32.034 --> 00:14:34.264
Congratulations.

00:14:34.302 --> 00:14:38.136
You almost wiped out...
8,000 civilizations.

00:14:40.709 --> 00:14:44.372
I didn't consider
the entire history of the comet.

00:14:44.413 --> 00:14:46.881
Four billion years ago,

00:14:46.915 --> 00:14:50.282
fragments from that comet
impacted a planet.

00:14:50.318 --> 00:14:53.412
Hydrocarbons from those
fragments gave rise to

00:14:53.455 --> 00:14:56.288
several species of plant life,
which in turn,

00:14:56.324 --> 00:14:57.484
sustained
more complex organisms.

00:14:57.559 --> 00:15:01.461
Ultimately, several
space-faring civilizations

00:15:01.496 --> 00:15:04.590
evolved and colonized
the entire sector.

00:15:04.633 --> 00:15:05.998
By erasing the comet,

00:15:06.034 --> 00:15:08.798
I altered all evolution
in this region.

00:15:08.837 --> 00:15:12.864
Past, present and future...

00:15:13.775 --> 00:15:15.606
they exist as one.

00:15:15.644 --> 00:15:17.874
They breathe together.

00:15:21.483 --> 00:15:23.781
You're not the only person
to make this mistake.

00:15:27.055 --> 00:15:30.889
When I first constructed
this weapon ship,

00:15:30.926 --> 00:15:34.089
I turned it against
our greatest enemy...

00:15:34.129 --> 00:15:35.562
the Rilnar.

00:15:37.899 --> 00:15:40.231
The result was miraculous.

00:15:40.268 --> 00:15:43.362
With the Rilnar
gone from history,

00:15:43.405 --> 00:15:47.307
my people, in an instant,
became powerful again,

00:15:47.342 --> 00:15:49.776
but there were problems.

00:15:51.379 --> 00:15:54.212
A rare disease broke out
among our colonies.

00:15:54.249 --> 00:15:56.979
Within a year,
50 million were dead.

00:15:57.018 --> 00:15:59.282
I had failed to realize
that the Rilnar

00:15:59.321 --> 00:16:01.789
had introduced
a crucial antibody

00:16:01.823 --> 00:16:03.791
into the Krenim genome...

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:09.960
and my weapon had eliminated
that antibody as well.

00:16:09.998 --> 00:16:12.398
And you've been trying to undo
that damage ever since,

00:16:12.434 --> 00:16:15.767
but each time
you pull out a new thread

00:16:15.804 --> 00:16:17.669
another one begins to unravel.

00:16:17.706 --> 00:16:21.142
You can't imagine the burden
of memory that I carry...

00:16:21.176 --> 00:16:23.701
thousands of worlds,

00:16:23.745 --> 00:16:25.770
billions of lives

00:16:25.814 --> 00:16:28.146
gone, brought back,

00:16:28.183 --> 00:16:30.117
gone again.

00:16:30.152 --> 00:16:33.280
I try to rationalize the loss.

00:16:33.321 --> 00:16:35.915
They're not
really being destroyed

00:16:35.957 --> 00:16:37.686
because they never existed.

00:16:39.494 --> 00:16:41.826
Sometimes I can...

00:16:41.863 --> 00:16:44.195
almost convince myself.

00:16:44.232 --> 00:16:46.598
You've been at this
for 200 years, Annorax.

00:16:46.635 --> 00:16:48.466
What makes you think
you're ever going to succeed?

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.471
What makes you think Voyager
will ever reach Earth?

00:16:51.573 --> 00:16:55.475
The odds against you
are astronomical.

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:58.536
Yet, you keep trying.

00:16:59.714 --> 00:17:02.410
You're right, but we
don't destroy everything

00:17:02.517 --> 00:17:03.984
that stands in our way.

00:17:04.019 --> 00:17:06.749
You can help me
to change that, Chakotay.

00:17:06.788 --> 00:17:10.724
Together, we'll restore
the Krenim and Voyager

00:17:10.759 --> 00:17:13.250
and we'll undo the damage
that I've caused.

00:17:14.529 --> 00:17:16.429
I've still got a lot to learn.

00:17:16.464 --> 00:17:17.863
Come.

00:17:17.899 --> 00:17:20.629
It's time I show you
the heart of this vessel...

00:17:20.669 --> 00:17:21.863
the temporal core.

00:17:35.317 --> 00:17:36.614
Engines?

00:17:36.651 --> 00:17:38.050
I'm doing my best!

00:17:38.086 --> 00:17:39.610
Captain,
with the deflector down,

00:17:39.654 --> 00:17:42.179
those micro-meteoroids
are beginning to erode the hull.

00:17:42.224 --> 00:17:44.021
Emergency power
to the deflector.

00:17:44.059 --> 00:17:45.026
None available.

00:17:47.863 --> 00:17:49.922
I'll be in Deflector Control.

00:17:49.965 --> 00:17:52.092
Captain, that entire section

00:17:52.133 --> 00:17:53.623
has been designated
hazard-level 4.

00:17:53.668 --> 00:17:54.726
I know.

00:18:11.486 --> 00:18:14.114
Oh, why do I get the feeling
you're testing me, Voyager?

00:18:14.155 --> 00:18:16.419
Bridge, there's a fire
in Deflector Control.

00:18:16.491 --> 00:18:17.890
Any luck with the engines?

00:18:17.926 --> 00:18:19.518
The warp core's still off-line.

00:18:19.561 --> 00:18:23.053
Micro-meteoroid density
is increasing.

00:18:25.367 --> 00:18:28.393
The nacelle pylon is buckling.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:36.768
Bridge, I'm going in.

00:18:36.811 --> 00:18:38.438
Stand by
to engage the deflector.

00:18:38.546 --> 00:18:40.571
Tell the Doctor I'll be coming
back with severe burns.

00:18:40.615 --> 00:18:41.582
Captain...

00:18:41.616 --> 00:18:42.708
Do it.

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:46.580
Be kind.

00:18:53.762 --> 00:18:56.253
The Captain's accessed
manual control.

00:18:56.298 --> 00:18:58.596
She's stabilizing
the particle emitters.

00:18:59.634 --> 00:19:00.601
She's got it.

00:19:00.635 --> 00:19:01.602
Deflector's on line.

00:19:01.636 --> 00:19:04.628
Activating deflector field.

00:19:04.673 --> 00:19:06.607
Bridge to Janeway.

00:19:09.477 --> 00:19:11.274
Captain, please respond.

00:19:57.125 --> 00:19:59.116
What's my condition?

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:00.957
You suffered
third-degree burns

00:20:00.996 --> 00:20:03.191
to approximately
60 percent of your body.

00:20:03.231 --> 00:20:05.131
I've healed most of them,

00:20:05.166 --> 00:20:06.656
but without
a dermal regenerator,

00:20:06.701 --> 00:20:09.192
I couldn't repair
all the damage to your skin.

00:20:09.237 --> 00:20:12.968
You've been left with scars
on your face and arms.

00:20:16.711 --> 00:20:18.941
I'll consider them mementos.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.641
Not so fast.

00:20:20.682 --> 00:20:23.480
You're spending the next
few days here with me.

00:20:23.585 --> 00:20:24.609
What for?

00:20:24.652 --> 00:20:25.619
Observation.

00:20:25.653 --> 00:20:27.177
Is there something else
wrong with me?

00:20:27.222 --> 00:20:28.189
Not physically.

00:20:28.223 --> 00:20:29.986
What are you suggesting?

00:20:30.025 --> 00:20:32.118
Traumatic stress syndrome.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.492
Symptoms: Irritability,
sleeplessness,

00:20:34.562 --> 00:20:37.122
obsessional thoughts,
reckless behavior...

00:20:37.165 --> 00:20:39.133
all of which
you've demonstrated

00:20:39.167 --> 00:20:40.225
over the last few weeks.

00:20:40.268 --> 00:20:44.398
My only obsession is
with saving my ship, my people.

00:20:44.439 --> 00:20:46.304
If I've been taking
some reckless chances

00:20:46.341 --> 00:20:48.809
in order to do that, it's
hardly a medical condition.

00:20:48.843 --> 00:20:50.435
I'm not going to stand
here while you rationalize

00:20:50.478 --> 00:20:51.467
yet another brush with death.

00:20:51.513 --> 00:20:52.480
You don't have to.

00:20:52.514 --> 00:20:53.503
As Chief Medical Officer,

00:20:53.615 --> 00:20:55.412
I have the authority
to relieve you of your command.

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:56.644
You're not going to do that.

00:20:56.684 --> 00:20:58.208
Lf, in my medical opinion,

00:20:58.253 --> 00:21:01.188
your judgment has been impaired,
I can and I will.

00:21:01.222 --> 00:21:04.749
Try it and I'll shut down
your program.

00:21:04.793 --> 00:21:06.454
That threat in itself

00:21:06.494 --> 00:21:09.156
is evidence
of your unstable condition.

00:21:10.598 --> 00:21:13.362
I am sorry, Doctor.

00:21:13.401 --> 00:21:15.995
I've been operating
on instinct for so long,

00:21:16.037 --> 00:21:17.800
I did not think before I spoke.

00:21:17.839 --> 00:21:20.672
I have no intention
of deactivating you,

00:21:20.708 --> 00:21:23.404
but I won't stay
in this Mess Hall.

00:21:23.445 --> 00:21:24.412
Is that final?

00:21:24.446 --> 00:21:25.413
Final.

00:21:25.447 --> 00:21:26.505
Then you leave me no choice.

00:21:27.549 --> 00:21:29.346
Captain Kathryn Janeway,

00:21:29.384 --> 00:21:31.716
under Starfleet Medical
Regulation 121, Section A,

00:21:31.753 --> 00:21:33.983
I, the Chief Medical Officer,
do hereby relieve you

00:21:34.022 --> 00:21:37.048
of your active command,
effective immediately.

00:21:38.193 --> 00:21:39.490
Have a seat.

00:21:39.561 --> 00:21:42.655
How do you plan to implement
this protocol, Doctor?

00:21:42.697 --> 00:21:46.463
Mr. Tuvok doesn't have
a security team;

00:21:46.501 --> 00:21:48.093
both the brigs
have been destroyed;

00:21:48.136 --> 00:21:50.229
and with the internal
force fields off-line,

00:21:50.271 --> 00:21:52.205
you'll have a hell of a time
keeping me confined.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.231
You'd better grab a phaser

00:21:54.275 --> 00:21:56.243
because
before I give up command,

00:21:56.277 --> 00:21:57.767
you'll have to shoot me.

00:21:59.447 --> 00:22:03.543
You realize this incident will
be noted in my official logs.

00:22:03.585 --> 00:22:06.748
By refusing my orders, you risk
a general court-martial.

00:22:06.788 --> 00:22:09.120
Compared to what I've been
through the past few months,

00:22:09.157 --> 00:22:13.025
a court-martial would be
a small price to pay.

00:22:14.596 --> 00:22:17.030
If we make it back home...

00:22:17.065 --> 00:22:19.056
I'll be happy to face the music.

00:22:34.015 --> 00:22:36.040
Another ruptured EPS conduit.

00:22:36.084 --> 00:22:37.051
32 so far.

00:22:37.085 --> 00:22:39.280
33, 34, 35...

00:22:39.321 --> 00:22:41.915
And that fluidic converter
needs to be purged.

00:22:41.957 --> 00:22:43.049
Right.

00:22:43.091 --> 00:22:45.321
The gravitational plating
in this room has buckled.

00:22:46.795 --> 00:22:48.490
Chakotay's quarters.

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:27.930
You disobeyed orders.

00:23:27.969 --> 00:23:29.095
Captain?

00:23:31.740 --> 00:23:34.641
Chakotay gave this
to me five months ago...

00:23:34.676 --> 00:23:36.769
a birthday gift.

00:23:39.247 --> 00:23:40.714
I ordered him to...

00:23:53.328 --> 00:23:55.057
What do you think?

00:23:55.096 --> 00:23:56.256
Handsome.

00:23:58.066 --> 00:23:59.294
Come on.

00:24:08.877 --> 00:24:10.344
Astounding.

00:24:10.378 --> 00:24:12.073
Not really.

00:24:12.113 --> 00:24:13.910
I get lucky now and again.

00:24:13.949 --> 00:24:16.611
Uh, your end game sequence,
it, uh...

00:24:16.651 --> 00:24:18.812
it was the same one
favored by my brother.

00:24:18.854 --> 00:24:22.153
To quote a long-lost friend
of mine:

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.215
"It seemed logical."

00:24:28.163 --> 00:24:29.494
Now what?

00:24:32.133 --> 00:24:36.194
I used to honor
the day of his birth.

00:24:36.238 --> 00:24:37.227
Who?

00:24:37.272 --> 00:24:39.365
My brother.

00:24:41.810 --> 00:24:44.176
And my parents,
my closest friends.

00:24:44.212 --> 00:24:46.476
Every year, at first.

00:24:46.514 --> 00:24:50.951
Then one day, I realized
a century had passed...

00:24:50.986 --> 00:24:54.149
and for years, I had been
celebrating birthdays...

00:24:57.292 --> 00:24:58.520
for the dead.

00:24:59.694 --> 00:25:01.355
Mmm.

00:25:01.396 --> 00:25:04.160
Or for people
who never even existed.

00:25:07.802 --> 00:25:09.201
I'm sorry.

00:25:16.278 --> 00:25:18.371
You can put that thing down,
Chakotay.

00:25:18.413 --> 00:25:20.847
No need to strain your eyes
anymore.

00:25:20.882 --> 00:25:22.008
I've got a plan.

00:25:22.050 --> 00:25:23.176
Let's hear it.

00:25:23.218 --> 00:25:24.446
This ship's temporal core

00:25:24.552 --> 00:25:26.417
keeps the vessel out of phase
with normal space-time,

00:25:26.454 --> 00:25:28.888
but its shields
are incredibly weak.

00:25:28.924 --> 00:25:31.916
You take that core off-line,
and a photon grenade

00:25:31.960 --> 00:25:33.655
could penetrate the hull.

00:25:33.695 --> 00:25:35.094
How do you know all this?

00:25:35.130 --> 00:25:38.861
I've been spending time
with our friend Obrist,

00:25:38.900 --> 00:25:41.460
who seems more than willing
to share information.

00:25:41.536 --> 00:25:43.470
And that's not all.

00:25:43.571 --> 00:25:45.903
Does the name Captain Bligh
mean anything to you?

00:25:45.941 --> 00:25:49.274
This is not a happy crew.

00:25:49.311 --> 00:25:50.972
They've been at this
for 200 years now.

00:25:51.012 --> 00:25:52.377
They're tired of it, Chakotay.

00:25:52.414 --> 00:25:53.403
They want it to end.

00:25:57.152 --> 00:25:58.813
Good work, Tom,

00:25:58.853 --> 00:26:00.821
but I'm not quite ready
to start a mutiny.

00:26:00.855 --> 00:26:02.288
Keep gathering information.

00:26:02.324 --> 00:26:03.757
Lie low.

00:26:03.792 --> 00:26:06.522
I'm starting to make progress
on the temporal calculations.

00:26:06.561 --> 00:26:08.426
With a little time and luck,

00:26:08.463 --> 00:26:10.795
I think we can get
the Krenim back on their feet

00:26:10.832 --> 00:26:13.130
and Voyager back
to the Alpha Quadrant.

00:26:13.168 --> 00:26:15.568
You're starting to sound
like Annorax...

00:26:15.603 --> 00:26:17.298
always one more calculation.

00:26:17.339 --> 00:26:18.533
This time it's going
to be perfect.

00:26:18.573 --> 00:26:19.562
This can work.

00:26:19.607 --> 00:26:21.006
If you'd take time to listen,

00:26:21.042 --> 00:26:23.067
you'd understand what Annorax
is trying to do.

00:26:23.111 --> 00:26:25.773
What? Wipe out civilizations
to help his own race?

00:26:25.814 --> 00:26:27.076
I understand perfectly.

00:26:27.115 --> 00:26:29.743
It's more complicated
than that.

00:26:32.187 --> 00:26:34.451
Annorax is an enlightened man...

00:26:34.489 --> 00:26:36.787
misguided, but I think
he wants this to end

00:26:36.825 --> 00:26:38.019
as much as anyone.

00:26:38.059 --> 00:26:41.460
I guess I don't have
the instinct for time...

00:26:41.496 --> 00:26:44.556
or whatever it is Captain Nemo
out there calls it.

00:26:44.599 --> 00:26:46.260
Chakotay, he's been
flattering you

00:26:46.301 --> 00:26:47.700
and it's gone to your head.

00:26:47.736 --> 00:26:49.169
You're out of line, Lieutenant.

00:26:51.940 --> 00:26:54.272
Maybe I shouldn't
start a mutiny,

00:26:54.309 --> 00:26:55.469
but I might be able
to get Obrist

00:26:55.577 --> 00:26:57.306
to help us send a message
to Captain Janeway.

00:26:57.345 --> 00:27:00.781
Not yet... if you get caught,
we lose everything.

00:27:00.815 --> 00:27:01.873
I can get us out of this.

00:27:01.916 --> 00:27:03.679
Not if I can get us
out of here first.

00:27:03.718 --> 00:27:06.653
You're not doing anything
against Annorax.

00:27:06.688 --> 00:27:08.383
That's an order.

00:27:10.125 --> 00:27:11.217
What are you going to do,

00:27:11.259 --> 00:27:12.692
take away
my holodeck privileges?

00:27:12.727 --> 00:27:16.185
Either we maintain
our command structure

00:27:16.231 --> 00:27:17.755
or else
we settle our differences

00:27:17.799 --> 00:27:18.891
the old-fashioned way.

00:27:24.305 --> 00:27:25.272
What's happening?

00:27:25.306 --> 00:27:27.103
We're preparing
for a temporal incursion.

00:27:27.142 --> 00:27:28.109
What incursion?

00:27:28.143 --> 00:27:29.132
You didn't say anything...

00:27:29.177 --> 00:27:30.439
I had an inspiration
last night.

00:27:30.478 --> 00:27:31.445
By my calculations,

00:27:31.479 --> 00:27:33.344
the eradication
of the Ram lzad species

00:27:33.381 --> 00:27:35.679
will result
in a 52 percent restoration

00:27:35.717 --> 00:27:37.116
of the Krenim timeline.

00:27:37.152 --> 00:27:39.211
I thought we were working
to avoid more destruction.

00:27:39.254 --> 00:27:41.381
When time offers you
an opportunity,

00:27:41.423 --> 00:27:42.981
you don't ignore it.

00:27:43.024 --> 00:27:45.356
We're within range
of their homeworld.

00:27:46.728 --> 00:27:48.093
Take us into orbit.

00:27:48.129 --> 00:27:49.619
Full power to the weapon.

00:27:49.664 --> 00:27:51.598
Prepare for total erasure.

00:27:52.801 --> 00:27:54.894
Is this what you call
enlightened?

00:27:54.936 --> 00:27:56.631
Targeting the focal point.

00:27:56.671 --> 00:27:58.866
Locked.

00:27:58.907 --> 00:28:00.772
Please, this isn't necessary.

00:28:00.809 --> 00:28:02.333
We'll find another way.

00:28:09.818 --> 00:28:11.251
Fire.

00:28:17.292 --> 00:28:18.759
Trace elements?

00:28:18.793 --> 00:28:21.159
Diminishing.

00:28:21.196 --> 00:28:22.993
Counter-indications.

00:28:23.031 --> 00:28:24.726
None so far.

00:28:24.766 --> 00:28:26.427
Scan the continuum.

00:28:26.534 --> 00:28:28.263
Bring me the results
once they're complete.

00:28:28.303 --> 00:28:29.270
Yes, sir.

00:28:29.304 --> 00:28:31.101
I'll be in my chambers.

00:28:36.044 --> 00:28:38.808
Have you seen enough
yet, Chakotay?

00:28:38.847 --> 00:28:42.476
If you don't do something
about this maniac, I will.

00:28:56.231 --> 00:28:58.222
You didn't need
to fire on that planet.

00:28:58.266 --> 00:29:02.293
I'm altering history
on a massive scale.

00:29:02.337 --> 00:29:05.670
The destinies of countless
star systems are in my hands.

00:29:05.707 --> 00:29:08.505
The fate of one species
is insignificant.

00:29:08.543 --> 00:29:10.773
You're trying
to rationalize genocide.

00:29:10.812 --> 00:29:12.404
One species is significant.

00:29:12.514 --> 00:29:14.345
A single life is significant.

00:29:19.788 --> 00:29:22.552
It seemed so...

00:29:22.591 --> 00:29:25.424
easy the first time.

00:29:25.460 --> 00:29:30.727
In the blink of an eye,
I had changed history itself,

00:29:30.765 --> 00:29:33.131
allowed my people
to thrive again.

00:29:35.704 --> 00:29:39.162
But when I changed history
a second time,

00:29:39.207 --> 00:29:42.233
I lost more
than you can imagine.

00:29:42.277 --> 00:29:44.211
The colony on Kyana Prime.

00:29:46.648 --> 00:29:48.275
How could you know that?

00:29:48.316 --> 00:29:51.774
I've been studying
your previous incursions.

00:29:51.820 --> 00:29:54.880
No matter how close you get
to restoring the timeline,

00:29:54.923 --> 00:29:57.221
one component
is always missing...

00:29:57.259 --> 00:29:58.783
Kyana Prime.

00:30:01.296 --> 00:30:03.093
Who was on that colony?

00:30:03.131 --> 00:30:05.224
Who did you lose?

00:30:05.267 --> 00:30:07.462
My wife...

00:30:07.569 --> 00:30:09.127
and with her, my future.

00:30:09.170 --> 00:30:12.469
My children, grandchildren...

00:30:12.574 --> 00:30:14.769
all erased because of me.

00:30:17.612 --> 00:30:19.876
This is all I have left of her.

00:30:19.915 --> 00:30:22.907
So many years
I worked through the night

00:30:22.951 --> 00:30:24.475
while she was sleeping.

00:30:24.519 --> 00:30:27.488
How could I have known I was...

00:30:27.522 --> 00:30:30.821
calculating her fate?

00:30:30.859 --> 00:30:34.852
I can't stop
until I've restored Kyana Prime

00:30:34.896 --> 00:30:37.091
and forced time
to give me back my wife.

00:30:37.132 --> 00:30:38.963
Maybe it isn't possible.

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:42.993
When I tell you
that time has moods...

00:30:43.038 --> 00:30:45.506
a disposition to be intuited...

00:30:45.540 --> 00:30:47.098
I'm not speaking metaphorically.

00:30:47.142 --> 00:30:48.609
What do you mean?

00:30:48.643 --> 00:30:50.907
Anger is one of its moods...

00:30:50.946 --> 00:30:53.938
anger and the desire for...

00:30:53.982 --> 00:30:56.951
retribution, vengeance.

00:30:56.985 --> 00:31:01.752
Time itself has tried
to punish me for my arrogance.

00:31:01.790 --> 00:31:05.123
It has kept me from my wife,
denied me my future.

00:31:06.294 --> 00:31:10.025
Sir, we've achieved
a 52 percent restoration.

00:31:10.065 --> 00:31:12.329
Kyana Prime?

00:31:13.401 --> 00:31:14.925
Negative, sir.

00:31:17.672 --> 00:31:20.004
Resume scanning the continuum.

00:31:20.041 --> 00:31:21.099
Yes, sir.

00:31:26.781 --> 00:31:28.442
I've, uh...

00:31:30.118 --> 00:31:31.915
I've studied your calculations,
Chakotay.

00:31:31.953 --> 00:31:35.980
They're promising...

00:31:36.024 --> 00:31:37.286
premature.

00:31:38.326 --> 00:31:40.021
We'll keep working on them.

00:31:40.061 --> 00:31:43.121
In the meantime,
my mission must continue.

00:31:43.164 --> 00:31:44.495
You don't have the right...

00:31:44.532 --> 00:31:45.999
To fight for what is mine?

00:31:46.034 --> 00:31:48.662
That's not for you to decide.

00:31:48.703 --> 00:31:52.537
Only time can pronounce
judgment against me.

00:31:59.614 --> 00:32:01.548
If that little display
doesn't convince you,

00:32:01.583 --> 00:32:02.641
I don't know what will.

00:32:02.684 --> 00:32:03.651
He's insane.

00:32:03.685 --> 00:32:04.845
No, he's not.

00:32:04.886 --> 00:32:05.978
Wounded maybe,

00:32:06.021 --> 00:32:08.546
even tortured,
but I can still reach him...

00:32:08.590 --> 00:32:09.750
convince him to stop.

00:32:09.791 --> 00:32:11.452
Not from what you've told me.

00:32:11.559 --> 00:32:15.928
This guy thinks that time has
a personal grudge against him.

00:32:15.964 --> 00:32:17.955
That's called paranoia,
Chakotay,

00:32:17.999 --> 00:32:19.398
with a hint of megalomania.

00:32:19.434 --> 00:32:20.833
You don't know
what he's been through.

00:32:21.970 --> 00:32:23.835
He's lost his family.

00:32:23.872 --> 00:32:25.134
Okay, that's a terrible thing,

00:32:25.173 --> 00:32:27.266
but so has everyone else
on this ship,

00:32:27.308 --> 00:32:29.003
and frankly, so have we!

00:32:32.714 --> 00:32:34.545
What kind of progress
have you made?

00:32:36.117 --> 00:32:38.449
Obrist is coming around...

00:32:38.486 --> 00:32:40.113
and I think we can trust him.

00:32:40.155 --> 00:32:43.488
He says he'll give me access
to their communications array.

00:32:43.525 --> 00:32:45.015
I can send a message to Voyager

00:32:45.060 --> 00:32:46.755
from the comfort
of my own quarters.

00:32:46.795 --> 00:32:48.956
And the temporal core?

00:32:48.997 --> 00:32:50.658
That's going to be
a little trickier.

00:32:50.698 --> 00:32:53.496
With Obrist's help, I'm
pretty sure I can disable it,

00:32:53.535 --> 00:32:57.027
but not without setting off
every alarm on this ship.

00:32:57.072 --> 00:32:58.903
We're only going
to have one chance.

00:32:58.940 --> 00:33:00.305
It'll require precise timing.

00:33:00.341 --> 00:33:01.899
You and me
working from within...

00:33:01.943 --> 00:33:04.776
And Captain Janeway
attacking from Voyager.

00:33:05.947 --> 00:33:09.815
That is...
if the Captain's still alive.

00:33:09.851 --> 00:33:11.182
She's alive.

00:33:14.923 --> 00:33:16.447
Send the message.

00:33:16.491 --> 00:33:17.549
Transmit our coordinates.

00:33:17.592 --> 00:33:18.559
Done.

00:33:18.593 --> 00:33:20.823
And...

00:33:20.862 --> 00:33:22.329
give Kathryn my best.

00:33:30.338 --> 00:33:34.468
Captain's Log, Stardate 51682.2.

00:33:34.576 --> 00:33:36.703
I've forged a coalition
with the Nihydron

00:33:36.744 --> 00:33:38.006
and the Mawasi.

00:33:38.046 --> 00:33:40.810
Together, we're preparing
to attack the weapon ship.

00:33:40.849 --> 00:33:43.113
I've analyzed
every carrier frequency

00:33:43.151 --> 00:33:44.482
of their transmission.

00:33:44.586 --> 00:33:48.682
It contains a classified
Starfleet ID code

00:33:48.723 --> 00:33:52.159
that could only have
come from Tom Paris.

00:33:52.193 --> 00:33:54.286
It's real.

00:33:54.329 --> 00:33:55.489
The coordinates he sent

00:33:55.563 --> 00:33:58.054
should lead us directly
to the weapon ship.

00:33:58.099 --> 00:33:59.066
Location?

00:33:59.100 --> 00:34:01.762
Approximately
50 light-years from here.

00:34:01.803 --> 00:34:05.102
Our new allies are
assembling reinforcements.

00:34:05.140 --> 00:34:07.973
Once we're in range,
Tom says he'll try

00:34:08.009 --> 00:34:10.443
to take the weapon ship
temporal core off-line.

00:34:10.545 --> 00:34:11.773
When that happens,

00:34:11.813 --> 00:34:13.713
they'll be vulnerable
to conventional weapons.

00:34:13.748 --> 00:34:17.650
Tom will then transmit
the exact location of the core.

00:34:17.685 --> 00:34:19.846
Our job will be
to disable the ship

00:34:19.888 --> 00:34:21.014
and get our people out.

00:34:21.055 --> 00:34:22.044
Is everyone clear?

00:34:22.090 --> 00:34:23.455
- Yes, ma'am.
- Aye, Captain.

00:34:24.726 --> 00:34:25.852
B'Elanna, Harry,

00:34:25.894 --> 00:34:27.623
I want you to beam over
to the Nihydron vessel.

00:34:27.662 --> 00:34:29.562
Work with their engineers.

00:34:29.597 --> 00:34:31.360
The entire fleet
needs to be equipped

00:34:31.399 --> 00:34:32.559
with temporal shielding.

00:34:32.600 --> 00:34:33.464
Aye, Captain.

00:34:33.568 --> 00:34:36.799
Tuvok, Neelix, Seven,

00:34:36.838 --> 00:34:38.465
you'll be working
on the Mawasi ship.

00:34:38.540 --> 00:34:39.564
Yes, Captain.

00:34:40.675 --> 00:34:43.200
Doctor, once the attack begins,

00:34:43.244 --> 00:34:46.475
your skills
will no doubt be required.

00:34:46.548 --> 00:34:47.879
Join Tuvok's team.

00:34:47.916 --> 00:34:49.247
What about yourself?

00:34:49.284 --> 00:34:51.980
I'll be piloting Voyager,
coordinating the attack.

00:34:52.020 --> 00:34:53.282
Captain,

00:34:53.321 --> 00:34:55.482
there's barely enough
of this ship left to get there,

00:34:55.557 --> 00:34:57.149
much less wage a war.

00:34:57.192 --> 00:34:59.319
There's fight in Voyager yet.

00:34:59.360 --> 00:35:01.487
It's still got
temporal shields...

00:35:01.529 --> 00:35:02.962
six photon torpedoes.

00:35:02.997 --> 00:35:04.760
It'll hold together.

00:35:04.799 --> 00:35:07.529
Besides, you know the adage...

00:35:07.569 --> 00:35:10.299
Captain goes down
with the ship, right?

00:35:10.338 --> 00:35:11.862
You have your orders.

00:35:12.974 --> 00:35:14.134
Dismissed.

00:35:27.655 --> 00:35:30.818
Tuvok, I can hear
your objections already.

00:35:30.858 --> 00:35:32.257
I am not leaving.

00:35:32.293 --> 00:35:34.693
Given Voyager's damaged state,

00:35:34.729 --> 00:35:36.856
the probability
of your surviving

00:35:36.898 --> 00:35:38.889
an armed conflict is marginal.

00:35:38.933 --> 00:35:42.562
Oh, I know the odds,
but I have to stay.

00:35:44.105 --> 00:35:46.198
Voyager's done too much for us.

00:35:48.409 --> 00:35:49.842
Curious.

00:35:49.877 --> 00:35:51.469
I have never understood
the human compulsion

00:35:51.512 --> 00:35:54.811
to emotionally bond
with inanimate objects.

00:35:54.849 --> 00:35:57.647
This vessel has done nothing.

00:35:57.685 --> 00:35:59.482
It is an assemblage

00:35:59.520 --> 00:36:02.956
of bulkheads, conduits,
tritanium...

00:36:02.991 --> 00:36:04.424
nothing more.

00:36:04.525 --> 00:36:06.015
Oh, you're wrong.

00:36:07.795 --> 00:36:10.662
It's much more than that.

00:36:10.698 --> 00:36:13.223
This ship has been our home.

00:36:13.268 --> 00:36:14.963
It's kept us together.

00:36:15.003 --> 00:36:17.437
It's been part of our family.

00:36:17.472 --> 00:36:20.202
As illogical
as this might sound...

00:36:20.241 --> 00:36:22.300
I feel as close to Voyager

00:36:22.343 --> 00:36:24.675
as I do to any other member
of my crew.

00:36:24.712 --> 00:36:26.612
It's carried us, Tuvok...

00:36:26.648 --> 00:36:30.084
even nurtured us...

00:36:30.118 --> 00:36:33.144
and right now,
it needs one of us.

00:36:34.722 --> 00:36:37.156
I respect your decision.

00:36:41.229 --> 00:36:43.925
Live long and prosper, Captain.

00:36:50.571 --> 00:36:51.629
Same to you...

00:36:53.174 --> 00:36:54.971
old friend.

00:38:02.609 --> 00:38:04.406
Voyager to Mawasi vessel.

00:38:04.478 --> 00:38:05.809
Go ahead, Captain.

00:38:05.846 --> 00:38:08.838
I'm picking up the weapon ship,
dead ahead.

00:38:08.882 --> 00:38:10.144
Confirmed.

00:38:10.183 --> 00:38:12.151
Temporal shields status.

00:38:12.185 --> 00:38:14.847
All vessels are bringing them
on line.

00:38:22.095 --> 00:38:24.029
This is Captain Janeway
to the fleet.

00:38:24.064 --> 00:38:26.862
Plot an intercept course
to the weapon ship.

00:38:30.504 --> 00:38:32.267
Sir, six vessels are
approaching our position.

00:38:32.305 --> 00:38:33.272
Identify.

00:38:33.306 --> 00:38:36.002
Three Nihydron warships,
two Mawasi cruisers...

00:38:36.042 --> 00:38:37.270
and Voyager.

00:38:38.545 --> 00:38:41.207
We're outside space-time,
impervious to their weapons.

00:38:41.248 --> 00:38:42.510
Let them come.

00:38:43.950 --> 00:38:45.110
I know Captain Janeway.

00:38:45.151 --> 00:38:46.448
She wouldn't be attacking

00:38:46.520 --> 00:38:48.545
unless she knew she
could do some damage.

00:38:53.360 --> 00:38:55.828
Good work, Obrist.

00:38:59.499 --> 00:39:01.967
If she's given the other
ships temporal shielding,

00:39:02.002 --> 00:39:03.936
they've undoubtedly
informed their homeworlds.

00:39:03.970 --> 00:39:06.905
They'll be able to protect their
planets against your weapon.

00:39:08.441 --> 00:39:10.841
Bring the weapon to full power.

00:39:10.877 --> 00:39:13.573
Stand by
for multiple incursions.

00:39:13.613 --> 00:39:17.845
We'll have to disable
their temporal shields first.

00:39:17.884 --> 00:39:20.717
Make the necessary calculations.

00:39:20.754 --> 00:39:23.154
All vessels report ready.

00:39:23.189 --> 00:39:25.714
Let's see if Tom
has done his part.

00:39:25.759 --> 00:39:28.250
Janeway to the fleet.

00:39:28.295 --> 00:39:30.923
Attack pattern omega.

00:39:30.964 --> 00:39:32.226
Engage.

00:39:38.772 --> 00:39:39.796
Condition?

00:39:39.839 --> 00:39:41.864
No damage.

00:39:41.908 --> 00:39:43.569
Temporal core is stable.

00:39:43.610 --> 00:39:44.907
Return fire.

00:39:51.418 --> 00:39:55.650
Captain, two Nihydron vessels
have been destroyed.

00:39:57.524 --> 00:39:58.752
Janeway to the fleet.

00:39:58.792 --> 00:40:01.556
Evasive pattern delta.
We're going to have to wait.

00:40:01.595 --> 00:40:03.187
Come on, Tom.
Come on.

00:40:05.398 --> 00:40:06.888
Target the other vessels.

00:40:13.707 --> 00:40:16.437
Obrist...
I said target the vessels.

00:40:23.984 --> 00:40:26.214
You're deactivating
the temporal core.

00:40:27.554 --> 00:40:29.249
I'm sorry, sir.

00:40:29.289 --> 00:40:30.586
It's over.

00:40:36.262 --> 00:40:38.230
Get back to your stations.

00:40:38.264 --> 00:40:40.129
You will not disobey me.

00:40:41.968 --> 00:40:44.596
We're phasing back
into normal space-time.

00:40:44.638 --> 00:40:47.971
Reconfigure
to conventional weapons.

00:40:49.643 --> 00:40:53.044
Captain, Chakotay and Paris
were beamed aboard our vessel.

00:40:53.079 --> 00:40:56.207
Everything's going as planned.

00:40:56.249 --> 00:40:57.682
Tom sent me the coordinates

00:40:57.717 --> 00:40:59.708
of their temporal core
before he left.

00:40:59.753 --> 00:41:03.416
I'm transmitting them
to you now.

00:41:03.456 --> 00:41:07.187
Conventional weapons are on line
and fully charged, sir.

00:41:07.227 --> 00:41:08.751
Fire at will!

00:41:58.511 --> 00:42:00.877
Sir, weapons are back
to full capacity.

00:42:00.914 --> 00:42:02.245
Target Voyager.

00:42:02.282 --> 00:42:05.080
Put Janeway out of her misery.

00:42:05.118 --> 00:42:07.814
All our ships
have been disabled, Captain.

00:42:07.854 --> 00:42:09.617
Do you have weapons?

00:42:09.656 --> 00:42:12.557
Negative.
Torpedo launchers are down.

00:42:12.592 --> 00:42:14.890
I'm setting a collision course.

00:42:17.063 --> 00:42:18.587
Janeway to the fleet.

00:42:18.631 --> 00:42:21.031
Take your temporal shields
off-line.

00:42:21.067 --> 00:42:22.830
Captain, we won't be protected.

00:42:22.869 --> 00:42:24.564
Exactly.

00:42:24.604 --> 00:42:26.162
If that ship is destroyed,

00:42:26.206 --> 00:42:28.936
all of history
might be restored,

00:42:28.975 --> 00:42:31.739
and this is one year
I'd like to forget.

00:42:36.483 --> 00:42:38.348
Time's... up.

00:42:56.703 --> 00:42:58.830
The core is destabilizing.

00:42:58.872 --> 00:43:00.305
It's going to cause
a temporal incursion

00:43:00.340 --> 00:43:01.432
within the ship.

00:43:24.697 --> 00:43:28.997
Captain's Log, Stardate 51252.3.

00:43:29.035 --> 00:43:31.162
The past couple of weeks
have been uneventful,

00:43:31.204 --> 00:43:32.432
but we've made
excellent progress

00:43:32.472 --> 00:43:34.736
on the new Astrometrics Lab.

00:43:34.774 --> 00:43:36.401
When can you bring it on line?

00:43:36.442 --> 00:43:38.376
We just did.

00:43:38.411 --> 00:43:41.471
In fact, we're in the process
of charting a new course home.

00:43:41.514 --> 00:43:43.573
I'd say this is cause
for celebration.

00:43:43.616 --> 00:43:45.982
A vessel is approaching
off the port bow, Captain.

00:43:46.019 --> 00:43:47.509
On screen.

00:43:49.222 --> 00:43:50.484
They're hailing us.

00:43:50.523 --> 00:43:51.581
Open a channel.

00:43:51.624 --> 00:43:54.991
You've entered Krenim space.

00:43:55.028 --> 00:43:56.689
State your identity.

00:43:56.729 --> 00:43:59.323
Captain Janeway
of the Starship Voyager.

00:43:59.365 --> 00:44:01.196
We're just passing through,
trying to get home.

00:44:01.234 --> 00:44:02.428
This region is in dispute.

00:44:02.502 --> 00:44:04.993
I suggest
you avoid our territory.

00:44:05.038 --> 00:44:06.596
Thanks for the warning.

00:44:06.639 --> 00:44:08.664
Good journey.

00:44:10.176 --> 00:44:12.644
Tom, plot a course
around Krenim space.

00:44:12.679 --> 00:44:14.112
Aye, sir.

00:44:14.147 --> 00:44:15.546
So what do you think?

00:44:15.582 --> 00:44:18.176
How about a ground-breaking
ceremony for our new lab?

00:44:18.218 --> 00:44:19.549
Sounds great.

00:44:19.586 --> 00:44:22.248
I think I'll replicate
a bottle of Saint Emilion

00:44:22.288 --> 00:44:23.414
for the occasion.

00:44:23.456 --> 00:44:27.825
2370...
I hear that was a good year.

00:44:32.999 --> 00:44:34.125
Good morning.

00:44:37.036 --> 00:44:38.367
Good morning.

00:44:42.175 --> 00:44:44.370
Join me for breakfast?

00:44:44.410 --> 00:44:45.877
In a little while.

00:44:45.912 --> 00:44:49.473
I still have a...
few more calculations.

00:44:49.549 --> 00:44:50.982
There are always

00:44:51.017 --> 00:44:53.110
"a few more calculations."

00:44:53.152 --> 00:44:55.677
It's a beautiful day.

00:44:55.722 --> 00:44:58.190
Spend it with me.

00:45:01.527 --> 00:45:03.256
I suppose I can make the time.
